# Droidworks U.S.A.

## Droid #1 — Build History & Milestone Record

**Date:** Friday, October 2, 2026
**Milestone:** First fully functioning integrated Droid #1 prototype

---

## 1. Executive Summary

As of October 2, 2026, Droidworks U.S.A. Droid #1 has progressed from a collection of individual sensor, display, and microcontroller experiments into a functioning integrated robotic system.

Droid #1 now has a Raspberry Pi 5 running ROS 2 as its central computing platform. Multiple Arduino-based sensor and display modules are connected through a powered USB hub. A dedicated Hardware Manager identifies those physical modules by persistent EEPROM device identity rather than relying on fixed USB port numbers. Individual ROS sensor entry nodes receive their assigned hardware from the Hardware Manager.

The droid currently senses its environment through multiple sensor systems, processes those inputs through ROS 2, generates higher-level motion/orientation and affect states, expresses those states through an onboard OLED "eyes" display, and simultaneously transmits internal state information wirelessly to an ESP32-based CYD operator/debug display.

The most important result is that the entire chain has now been demonstrated successfully:

**Physical sensors → USB/MCU layer → Hardware Manager → ROS 2 entry nodes → fusion/state processing → affect → physical OLED expression → wireless CYD visualization**

This establishes Droid #1 as a functioning integrated prototype rather than simply a collection of working subsystems.

The CYD currently functions as a supplemental observation/debug interface. The architecture also provides a clear path toward eventually adding operator controls such as sliders, counters, parameter adjustments, overrides, and direct behavioral commands.

