# 2. Overall System Architecture

The current architecture is centered on the Raspberry Pi 5, referred to as **pi500**, running ROS 2.

```text
                         DROID #1
                             │
                     Raspberry Pi 5
                         ROS 2
                             │
                     Powered USB Hub
                ┌────────────┼────────────┐
                │            │            │
             Sensor        Display       Other
              MCUs           MCU          USB
                │
        Hardware Manager
                │
        Device Identity Map
                │
       ┌────────┼─────────┐
       │        │         │
      PIR      RCWL    Distance
       │        │      Sensors
       │        │       │    │
       └────────┴───────┴────┘
                  │
             ROS 2 State
                  │
             Affect System
             / OLED Logic
                  │
          ┌───────┴────────┐
          │                │
      Physical OLED       CYD
       Droid Eyes      Debug/Operator
```

The key architectural decision made during this phase was to establish the **Hardware Manager as the single hardware-discovery authority**.

Instead of every sensor node attempting to independently scan the USB hub, the Hardware Manager discovers the connected devices once, associates each device's persistent EID with its current Linux serial port, and publishes that information to the rest of the ROS system.

This greatly simplifies the entry-node architecture and eliminates dependence on changing `/dev/ttyUSB#` assignments.

