# 6. The USB Port Assignment Problem

One of the early problems exposed by the project was the instability of Linux USB serial numbering.

Devices could appear as:

```text
/dev/ttyUSB0
/dev/ttyUSB1
/dev/ttyUSB2
...
```

but their assignments changed after disconnect/reconnect events and hub power cycles.

At one point the ToF device existed as a different `/dev/ttyUSB#` than it had previously.

This demonstrated why hard-coded port assignments were unsuitable for the final architecture.

The EID-based Hardware Manager solved this by changing the relationship from:

**"this sensor is always ttyUSB4"**

to:

**"this EID is currently ttyUSB4."**

That is a much more robust model for a modular physical robot.

