# 7. USB Hub / CH340 Failure

Another significant hardware problem occurred during development.

The USB subsystem showed six CH340 USB converters but, at one point, only five usable `/dev/ttyUSB*` devices.

Investigation of the Linux device state showed that one serial device existed at the kernel/sysfs level but had failed to create a usable device node.

The kernel log reported:

```text
ch341-uart: probe of ttyUSB5 failed with error -32
```

There was also visible disconnect/reconnect activity.

The practical solution was to **power-cycle the powered USB hub**.

After the hub reset, all six CH340 devices appeared correctly:

```text
/dev/ttyUSB0
/dev/ttyUSB1
/dev/ttyUSB2
/dev/ttyUSB3
/dev/ttyUSB4
/dev/ttyUSB5
```

The Hardware Manager subsequently discovered all six devices successfully.

This incident reinforced an important lesson for the build:

**USB enumeration problems can masquerade as software or sensor failures.**

