# 12. Orientation System

The orientation module combines several inputs:

* MPU-6050 acceleration data
* tilt switch
* shock switch

The raw MCU telemetry looks like:

```text
TILT:0 SHOCK:0 AX:0.11 AY:0.01 AZ:0.98
```

The ROS entry node calculates orientation from the gravity vector.

Roll is calculated from:

```python
atan2(ay, az)
```

Pitch is calculated from:

```python
atan2(-ax, sqrt(ay² + az²))
```

The system publishes:

```text
/orientation_x
/orientation_y
/tilt_state
/shock_state
/accel_x
/accel_y
/accel_z
```

A higher-level orientation state node then determines whether the droid is upright or tilted.

The orientation state logic uses hysteresis:

* Enter TILTED at approximately 15°
* Return to UPRIGHT at approximately 10°

This prevents rapid state oscillation near the transition threshold.

The orientation system was physically tested and confirmed to register both orientation changes and upright/tilted state.

