# 15. Affect System

The existing affect architecture was deliberately preserved rather than redesigned during this integration phase.

The affect node subscribes to motion/fusion information and produces the current droid affect state.

The system currently defines states including:

```text
CALM
ALERT
FOCUSED
WARY
GUARDED
```

The current working logic actively maps the primary demonstrated states:

```text
CALM
ALERT
FOCUSED
```

and exposes:

```text
/droid_affect
/oled_expr
/oled_summary
```

The affect system was tested with live sensor activity.

The important milestone was that the affect state propagated all the way to physical behavior:

```text
Sensor activity
    ↓
ROS state/fusion
    ↓
Affect
    ↓
OLED expression
```

The physical OLED was observed changing among **CALM, ALERT, and FOCUSED** in response to the droid's environment.

That was the first direct demonstration of a complete perception-to-expression pipeline.

