# 16. CYD Wireless Debug / Operator Surface

The project also established an ESP32-based CYD display as a wireless supplemental interface.

The CYD is intentionally not the droid's brain.

Its current role is to provide an external window into the internal ROS/MQTT state of the droid.

The CYD includes pages for areas such as:

```text
Overview
Affect
Motion
Orientation
Radar
System
```

The orientation page provides a graphical representation of roll and pitch, along with state indicators.

The radar page uses a configured maximum range of 100 cm.

Touch navigation has been implemented, allowing a stylus or finger to move between display pages.

The wireless interface receives status from the Raspberry Pi through the MQTT-based debug/status channel.

After correcting the ToF message-type mismatch, the CYD became functional alongside the complete sensor stack.

